From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 15:54:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08533/11362] fix(arc): plan steps record real transitions;
 level-up/stall reinduction plans from current grid

Continues the 2026-08-08 adversarial live-agent review fix pass
(docs/research-notes/live-agent-adversarial-review-2026-08-08.md).

REQ-ARC-WMTE-6223 (Correctness finding 1): plan-step execution was fully
open-loop -- next_move()'s two plan-step branches never populated self._prev,
so a plan-won level's _win_transition read a stale pre-plan explore row
instead of the real winning step. Fixed via _track_prev_for_transition,
mirroring the explore branch's own bookkeeping.

REQ-ARC-WMTE-6224 (Correctness finding 2, plus a hostile-verifier-found gap):
level-up reinduction planned from self.root_grid (the level's opening grid)
even when _execute_plan_from_current=True replays the plan with no reset --
wrong from step 0, since a level-up reinduction only fires after the agent
has already moved. Fixed via a _plan_start_grid local. The first pass of this
fix scoped the swap to the level_up_reinduction branch only, on the claim
that _execute_plan_from_current is "guaranteed False" elsewhere. A hostile
verifier found that false: _observe_active_probe_transition can re-enter
induction (phase="induce" set directly) without going through either of
next_move()'s two reset sites, so the STALL path can be reentered with the
flag still True -- concretely, the active-probe disambiguation loop's own
plan does exactly this after observing its outcome. Closed by swapping the
remaining STALL-path root_grid reads too and correcting the now-false
comment. Bounded: only reachable when CARNOT_ARC_ACTIVE_PROBE=1 (default
off), so the default scored path was never affected.

Tests: test_arc_plan_execution_transition_capture_20260808.py (4 tests),
test_arc_level_up_reinduction_plan_start_grid_20260808.py (5 tests, incl. a
new reentry-mechanism test and a new STALL-path reentry regression test).
Broader sweep: 75 passed / 5 pre-existing environment skips across the
arc_competition_agent/active_probe/stall/level_up/plan_execution/
trajectory_transfer/early_stop/induce_think test areas.

Also acknowledges 12 results/ artifacts flagged stale by the artifact-
freshness-lint (this edit touches arc_competition_agent.py, which they
declare as a code dependency). Each acknowledgement is backed by a grep-
checked or self-measured reachability argument, not a blanket claim: most
either never construct E3AgentPolicy, or run with CARNOT_ARC_DISABLE_
INDUCTION=1 set before construction (so _induce_and_plan bails before
_plan_start_grid is ever computed), or -- for the one genuinely live-LLM
artifact -- the artifact's own recorded data shows zero induction attempts
across every cell of every arm. Two of the twelve are a second-order cascade
(an artifact citing two others by content hash, whose hashes moved only
because of their own new acknowledgement entries).

